{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"222ece408dd69c6ab71291cafb4211c7daf2f8f4fe807df4117c0fe8685de9ce","digest":{"component_or_area":"Jira label sanitization","key_entities":["JIRA_LABEL_MAX_CHARS","sanitize_label","sanitize_summary","InvalidLabelError","adapters/jira_family/sanitizers.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_backend_characterization.py","tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_dc_backend_characterization.py","tests/scripts/bridge/test_bridge_acli_field_coverage.py","test_the_instance_label_ceiling_measured_at_254_and_255","[tool.rebar.reconciler].comment_max_chars"],"problem_keywords":["label ceiling","jira cloud","jira data center","character limit","validation","sanitization"],"propositions":["Jira DC and Cloud both accept 255-character labels and reject 256-character labels; the reported divergence (DC 254 vs Cloud 255) does not exist.","sanitize_label raises InvalidLabelError above the ceiling without truncating, while sanitize_summary truncates with a visible suffix; this divergence is deliberate because labels are identity tokens and truncation would invent a different label.","The shared JIRA_LABEL_MAX_CHARS constant set to 255 is correct for both Cloud and DC deployments and requires no per-deployment override.","Measurement via live probes against navasage.atlassian.net (Cloud) and harness run 30951453979 (DC) confirms identical behavior: 255 accepted with byte-exact round-trip, 256 rejected with HTTP 400."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787878413614647001,"uuid":"2654d47e-ee95-4c09-9f57-53448c40294e"}